<title>BAHRAIN: Saudi Bank Al-Jazira 1996 net rises to $3.7 mln.</title>
<headline>Saudi Bank Al-Jazira 1996 net rises to $3.7 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		    (million Saudi riyals)</p>
<p> Share			 2.34 riyals  vs	0.08 riyals</p>
<p> Net profit		 14.0	    vs	0.458</p>
<p> Net operating income   13.15	   vs	1.67 (loss)</p>
<p> Other income		0.86	   vs	2.13</p>
<p> Shareholders funds    521.4	    vs    507.4</p>
<p> Customer deposits   1,808.8	    vs  1,598.1</p>
<p> Assets		  4,439.7	    vs  4,713.7</p>
<p>Full Name: Bank Al-Jazira</p>
<p>Note - The Jeddah-based bank, traded in the Saudi market, is 5.83 percent owned by National Bank of Pakistan. The rest is held by Saudi Arabian investors. ($1=3.75 riyals) -- Manama newsroom 973-536187</p>
</text>
